msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-frame-setup.rst:96
#: 7135521e6163438588339c803a741d2b
msgid "The normal plane outputs are assumed to be on 1 to 4 as usual. Only vertical lift outputs (5 to 8 on a quad setup) normally should be run at high PWM rate (400Hz). When using these default configurations, you can assign other outputs to whatever functions you desire."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-frame-setup.rst:100
#: bc06ae3480c2480d9041fd55a46e68d7
msgid "You can optionally move the motors to be on any other channel, using the procedure outlined in the section further below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-frame-setup.rst:103
#: b59c104afd1c43d59773cf4a5acd15e3
msgid "Tricopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-frame-setup.rst:105
#: 92b02aa8e54c4e9f9e1d2048b7b3b95f
msgid "Frame Type 7 is Tricopter and can be either non-Tiltrotor, or a :ref:`Tiltrotor<guide-tilt-rotor>` configuration for the front motors, but using a separate servo to sideways tilt the rear motor for yaw control, or a :ref:`Tiltrotor<guide-tilt-rotor>` using Vectored Yaw control via the front tilting motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-frame-setup.rst:107
#: 41e236a885b447e29a49f2887ed4d15d
msgid "If using a tilting yaw control, an output is setup as Motor 7 (``SERVOn_FUNCTION`` = 39) for a servo-controlled sideways tilt mechanism for the yaw motor, Motor 4. You should set up the yaw servo’s maximum lean angle in degrees with :ref:`Q_M_YAW_SV_ANGLE<Q_M_YAW_SV_ANGLE>` to prevent prop strikes to the ground or frame. This lean angle assumes that ``SERVOn_MIN`` and ``SERVOn_MAX``, represent +/- 90 degrees, with ``SERVOn_TRIM`` representing 0 degrees lean."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-frame-setup.rst:109
#: f4dc9b2e1bf647cf908330e75c85c958
msgid "the rear motor tilt servo is not affected by :ref:`Q_TILT_MASK<Q_TILT_MASK>` or any other :ref:`Tiltrotor<guide-tilt-rotor>` related parameters since it is not involved with vertical or horizontal propulsion, only yaw control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-frame-setup.rst:112
#: 441f69c09070427dbd8abe2d8d569a14
msgid "Tilt-Rotors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-frame-setup.rst:114
#: 86e454af0da546848c6843b6c32e8bab
msgid "See :ref:`guide-tilt-rotor`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-frame-setup.rst:117
#: 91c216bc586247ce91fdeac59cb991de
msgid "Using different channel mappings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-frame-setup.rst:119
#: 181dcdde924f48ee8e0b18f9f5e04e86
msgid "You can remap what output channels the lifting motors are on by setting values for SERVOn_FUNCTION. This follows the same approach as :ref:`other output functions <common-rcoutput-mapping>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-frame-setup.rst:123
#: 85ed0cd28fc6433692ad0f118c501c24
msgid "Note that you do not need to set any of the SERVOn_FUNCTION values unless you have a non-standard motor ordering, using vectored thrust, or are a Tailsitter. It is highly recommended that you use the standard ordering and do not set the SERVOn_FUNCTION parameters, leaving them at zero. They will be automatically set to the right values for your frame on boot."
msgstr ""

